        "counter": "The Services gross margin thesis relies heavily on frictionless monetization that is currently under acute regulatory siege [Interpretation]. The US DOJ antitrust lawsuit, EU Digital Markets Act (DMA) enforcement, and potential remedies from the DOJ v. Google antitrust ruling directly imperil Google's estimated ~$20B annual Search Traffic Acquisition Costs (TAC) paid to Apple [Estimate], which flow through at near 100% gross margin [Fact]. Slicing or eliminating Google TAC, combined with mandated alternative app marketplaces and fee caps in Europe [Fact], threatens to compress Services margins and erase the projected 150-250 bps corporate gross margin expansion [Estimate]."
